{"status": "completed", "battle": "B5/R1", "weighted_error_reduction_vs_prior": 0.36053391864399564, "actor_gain_vs_prior": 3.3989303325931974e-05, "derivation": "BCE contrast is softplus(z_alt)-softplus(z_factual)-q*(z_alt-z_factual). Halfblend uses .5*y+.5*q, so residual squared is .25*(q-y)^2*(z_alt-z_factual)^2. Therefore 4*sum(residual squared)/sum(logit gap squared) reconstructs sensitivity-weighted Brier. Exact arm uses y, hence zero teaching residual does not imply perfect issued outcome prediction.", "scope": "Completed exploratory eight-case cohort. Arms share incoming learner but diverge during adaptation; weighted errors use each arm own routes, not paired fixed-route causal effects. Logit-gap weighting is immediate loss sensitivity, not optimizer/future-learning sensitivity. No new fit, task advantage, audit saving or efficiency claim."}
